From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: KintTany port maintainer <patches@localhost>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 22:20:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] BladesTime: provide offline resolver h_errno without sfdnsres

Run 44844936301 got beyond the previous Nintendo ec abort, initialized
an empty offline consumable manager, loaded the profile and built the
Dagor main-menu level. The game next attempted matchmaking at
xb2-match-01.bladesoftime.com:7870 and crashed in SDK 9.4
at sdk+0xf75dc (ldr x8,[x8]) with x8 == 0.

Reverse-engineering the actual sdk.patched.bin PLT chain:
  sdk+0xef178 → nn::socket::resolver::tls::Client::InternalHostErrno
  sdk+0xf9704 → nn::socket::resolver::tls::Client::GetCreateClientTLS
  sdk+0xf75bc → nn::socket::resolver::tls::GetCreateTLSPair
The SDK tries to get resolver TLS from a missing Nintendo DNS session,
receives Result 0x7fe03 and then dereferences its null pointer.

The host's existing hle_net.c already returns offline network errors for
DNS requests. Supply an addressable per-thread h_errno with NO_RECOVERY=3
so the guest handles the failed resolution instead of crashing in SDK
TLS. This changes neither network state nor ownership, and never fakes
a server or connection. Other sockets continue to use t_skerr.

Upstream-Status: fork-only
Reason: fix real BladesTime menu SDK9.4 offline DNS null resolver TLS crash
Issue: joao9vegeto-stack/KintTany BladesTime run 44844936301
---
 dm/host/hle_net.c | 13 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+)

diff --git a/dm/host/hle_net.c b/dm/host/hle_net.c
--- a/dm/host/hle_net.c
+++ b/dm/host/hle_net.c
@@ -38,7 +38,21 @@
 // this service, not Darwin's fd table, and stay small enough for games' fd_set arrays. Address/flag/error constants below are the Horizon/FreeBSD ABI (libnx's BSD service passes
 // these structures/flags unchanged; FreeBSD11 sys/socket.h and netinet/in.h). IPv4 payloads retain packet boundaries; the per-endpoint queue holds at most256 packets/1MiB.
 #define SK_ENETDOWN 50
 static __thread int t_skerr = SK_ENETDOWN;
+// Nintendo SDK 9.4 still calls resolver::tls::Client::InternalHostErrno
+// when an offline lookup fails. Its original implementation tries to get
+// a resolver TLS service session; with no sfdnsres session it returns
+// 0x7fe03 and dereferences a NULL TLS pair at sdk+0xf75dc. This is a
+// thread-local HOST error number (h_errno), distinct from the BSD errno.
+static __thread int t_sk_herrno = 3;  // NO_RECOVERY: no offline DNS service.
+HLE_FORCE("_ZN2nn6socket8resolver3tls6Client17InternalHostErrnoEv",
+          "offline resolver h_errno: thread-local no-recovery rather than missing TLS session",
+          int *, h_sk_ResolverHostErrno, void) {
+    static _Atomic int logged;
+    if (!atomic_exchange(&logged, 1))
+        LOG("socket: offline resolver TLS host errno available (NO_RECOVERY, no network)");
+    return &t_sk_herrno;
+}
 static int sk_error(int error) { t_skerr = error; return -1; }
 static int sk_fail(void) { return sk_error(SK_ENETDOWN); }
 int dm_sk_errno(void) { return t_skerr; }

